WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:02.868
-Today is Veterans Day, and we
wanted to do something special

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:05.037
to honor all those
who have served our country.

00:00:05.037 --> 00:00:06.605
So we have
an announcement to make.

00:00:06.605 --> 00:00:08.775
We here at "The Tonight Show"
have chosen to donate

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:11.044
to one of our favorite
veterans' charities,

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:12.745
the Fisher House Foundation,

00:00:12.745 --> 00:00:15.782
in the amount of $150,000.

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:20.086
♪♪

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:22.922
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:27.493 --> 00:00:29.395
The Fisher House --
If you don't know,

00:00:29.395 --> 00:00:30.797
the Fisher House
provides housing

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:33.132
for families
of military and veterans

00:00:33.132 --> 00:00:35.034
while their loved one
is receiving treatment.

00:00:35.034 --> 00:00:36.403
It's a great organization.

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:38.972
We're so proud
to give back to them.

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:40.807
But there's one more thing
we wanted to mention.

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:43.142
Our friends at
the Home Depot Foundation

00:00:43.142 --> 00:00:47.013
started a brand-new contest this
year called "Operation Surprise"

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:48.381
where people
all across the country

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:51.184
get to nominate
a U.S. military veteran in need.

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:55.788
And the winner gets $25,000 to
go toward critical home repairs.

00:00:55.788 --> 00:00:57.924
It's a great thing. And I'm
happy to say that the winner

00:00:57.924 --> 00:00:59.959
of this year's "Operation
Surprise" contest

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:01.561
is here with us tonight.

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:02.862
They're sitting in our audience,

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:06.165
and they have no idea
that they have been chosen.

00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:08.535
♪♪

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:10.536
-Ooh.

00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:12.572
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:20.413
♪♪

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:22.081
Oh!

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:29.722
♪♪

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:32.024
[ People speaking indistinctly ]

00:01:32.024 --> 00:01:34.927
♪♪

00:01:34.927 --> 00:01:36.795
-Is Vernita here?

00:01:36.795 --> 00:01:39.298
Is Vernita Love here?

00:01:39.298 --> 00:01:40.800
[ Audience "aww"s ]

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.136
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:46.405 --> 00:01:47.974
Can you stand up?

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:50.910
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.879
Can you stand up?

00:01:56.915 --> 00:01:58.617
You can stand up, too.

00:01:58.617 --> 00:02:00.486
Vernita?

00:02:00.486 --> 00:02:02.021
Vernita Love?

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:04.090
[ Laughing ]

00:02:07.426 --> 00:02:09.662
Vernita, I'm so happy.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.664
[ Laughing ]

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:14.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:17.904
This is going to get good.
This is going to get good.

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:20.673
This is only going
to get better.

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:22.474
Vernita --
-My eyelashes --

00:02:22.474 --> 00:02:24.811
-[ Laughs ] It's alright.

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:26.746
-I got to make sure
my eyelashes --

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:29.782
-Your eyelashes are still on.
Yeah, your eyelashes --

00:02:29.782 --> 00:02:32.084
Can we make sure her eyelashes
are still on?

00:02:32.084 --> 00:02:34.287
Vernita, is this your son Aaron?
-Yes.

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:36.388
-Aaron is the one
who nominated you.

00:02:36.388 --> 00:02:37.590
[ Audience "aww"s ]

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.592
Aaron, can you tell me
a little bit about --

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:41.093
Tell me a little bit
about your mom.

00:02:41.093 --> 00:02:43.062
-Yeah, my mother, man. She's --

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:45.431
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:50.403
Single mother from the East Side
of Detroit, Michigan, man.

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:52.505
She's raised me by herself.

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.640
She served 26 years
in the Air Force.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:58.677
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:58.677 --> 00:03:00.380
She's --

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:06.619
She's -- She's retired.

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:07.820
But at the same time, man,

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:09.788
I don't know anybody
more selfless than her.

00:03:09.788 --> 00:03:11.858
I mean, she'll give her last
to make somebody else good.

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:14.159
I mean, she gives
to the homeless vets in our area

00:03:14.159 --> 00:03:16.462
and is always constantly trying
to do things in the community.

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:19.698
I entered her in the contest
because her house is home,

00:03:19.698 --> 00:03:21.367
but behind the scenes, man,
it's a wreck, man.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:22.602
The electrical on it is old.

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:25.138
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.339 --> 00:03:29.175
-It's not that bad.

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:32.544
It's a beautiful place.

00:03:32.544 --> 00:03:34.547
-But I try to help out.
But, I mean, this $25,000

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:36.181
would definitely help out
in a long way.

00:03:36.181 --> 00:03:39.251
-As the winner,
you will be receiving $25,000

00:03:39.251 --> 00:03:41.620
for repairs for your home.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:45.357
And we actually have
one more surprise for you.

00:03:45.357 --> 00:03:48.294
Although $25,000 would really
help, after hearing your story,

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:51.196
the Home Depot Foundation
is doubling the prize

00:03:51.196 --> 00:03:53.266
in partnership with the --

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:56.168
You'll be receiving $50,000.

00:03:56.168 --> 00:03:59.972
♪♪

00:03:59.972 --> 00:04:02.007
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:02.007 --> 00:04:05.244
Get those eyelashes off!

00:04:05.244 --> 00:04:07.279
-Did they fall out?
-No, no.

00:04:07.279 --> 00:04:08.447
Here, please, have a seat.

00:04:08.447 --> 00:04:09.782
I don't want you falling down.

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:11.451
I love you.
Have a seat right there.

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:13.752
Enjoy yourself.
Aaron, here. Take care -- Yeah,

00:04:13.752 --> 00:04:15.788
and make sure those eyelashes
don't fall out.

00:04:15.788 --> 00:04:17.823
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.823 --> 00:04:19.225
Congratulations to you.

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:21.360
Thank you to
the Home Depot Foundation.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:22.528
Aaron, you're a good son.

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:24.263
-Thank you.
-Thank you, buddy.

00:04:24.263 --> 00:04:26.532
Thank you to
the Home Depot Foundation.

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:28.601
And thank you for your service.

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.002
I'm so happy. Stick around.

00:04:30.002 --> 00:04:32.238
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show," everybody.

